# Copy this file to .env (or run `python3 scripts/dnsctl.py setup`, which
# does this for you). Never commit .env - it's already in .gitignore.
#
# This project's PowerDNS provider doesn't use this value at all - its
# credential is the static apiKey already in creds.json. CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
# is only here because dnsctl.py's doctor/preview/push/begin commands are
# the real production script and hard-check for this exact variable name
# before running dnscontrol, regardless of which provider dnsconfig.js
# actually points at. Any non-empty value satisfies that check.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=local-placeholder-not-a-real-token

# submit/status/review/merge/validate need the GitHub CLI once this repo
# lives on github.com/<you>/<repo> - install it (https://cli.github.com/)
# and run `gh auth login` once. dnsctl.py shells out to `gh` automatically;
# there's no separate token to put here.
